	"title"		"More Network Capacity Renew by NgocDuy"
	"description"		"[h1]✨ WHAT'S NEW IN v4.3.43 (TM:PE Crash Immunization, Full Feature Save/Load & 256-Frame NetAI Stepper) ✨[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]TM:PE Save/Load Deserialization Crash Immunization (Zero Hooks into TM:PE):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Fixed the critical issue where TM:PE threw [i]IndexOutOfRangeException[/i] in [i]ParkingRestrictionsManager.LoadData[/i] when loading segments ≥ 36,864, triggering the TM:PE fatal error popup and causing ALL TM:PE settings across the city to be dropped.
    [*] Pre-expands [i]ParkingRestrictionsManager.parkingAllowed[/i] and all TM:PE simulation arrays to 65,024 via vanilla [i]SerializableDataWrapper.LoadData[/i] hook (strictly zero Harmony hooks into TM:PE methods).
[/list]
[*] [b]Comprehensive TM:PE Feature Preservation Across Savegames (Binary Payload v2):[/b]
[list]
    [*] [b]Timed Traffic Lights:[/b] Inspects all nodes [i]0..65,023[/i], saving all step timers, min/max times, and segment lights for low-ID + high-ID, high-ID + high-ID, and single nodes. Fixed [i]CustomSegmentLight[/i] instantiation via parameterless constructor.
    [*] [b]All Other TM:PE Tools Saved & Restored:[/b] Lane Connections, Custom Lane Speed Limits, Lane Arrows, Vehicle Restrictions, Junction Restrictions (U-Turn, Enter Blocked Junction, Pedestrian Crossing, Straight Lane Changing), Priority Signs, and Parking Restrictions.
[/list]
[*] [b]Fixed Default Traffic Lights Gridlock & Traffic Congestion Colors (256-Frame Stepper):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Corrected upper NetAI simulation stepping cadence to the exact vanilla 256-frame cycle ([i]frame = sm.m_currentFrameIndex & 255[/i]):
        - [b]Upper Nodes (32,768..65,023):[/b] Stepped at 126 nodes/frame. Default vanilla traffic lights now cycle at normal, realistic intervals, eliminating traffic light gridlock.
        - [b]Upper Segments (36,864..65,023):[/b] Stepped at 110 segments/frame. [i]m_trafficBuffer[/i] accumulates vehicles across the full 256 frames, allowing congested roads to reach high density and display vibrant RED in the traffic overlay!
    [*] TM:PE Timed Traffic Lights step at native 64-frame cadence (504 nodes/frame).
[/list]
        - [b]Toggle Traffic Lights, Speed Limits, & Parking Restrictions:[/b] Cached view overlays extended to 65K elements for seamless visual editing.
[/list]
[*] [b]High-ID TM:PE Savegame Serialization (SerializableDataExtensionBase):[/b]
[list]
    [*] TM:PE's own serializable data provider iterates nodes 0..32,767 when writing to savegames.
    [*] Implemented [i]MNCSerializableData[/i] using Cities: Skylines official [i]SerializableDataExtensionBase[/i] to cleanly serialize and restore custom junction restrictions, priority signs, and timed traffic lights for high-ID nodes (32,768..65,023) across save/load cycles with strictly zero hooks.
[/list]
[*] [b]100% Zero-Hook TM:PE Architecture Maintained:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Strictly [b]ZERO[/b] Harmony hooks into TM:PE methods. All synchronization and serialization are performed via managed threading extensions, official serializable data extensions, and variable expansion to guarantee pure native performance, zero desync, and zero crashes.
[/list]
[*] [b]Retains Universal Economy & Public Transport Protection (from v4.3.41):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Non-negative shields on [i]EconomyManager[/i], [i]SanitizeEconomy[/i] save repair, and [i]SanitizeTransportLines[/i] remain fully active to guard city funds.
[/list]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NETWORK CAPACITY RENEW[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Network Capacity Renew[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable legacy experimental versions that caused fatal crashes and corrupted traffic, [b]Renew[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536) and lanes up to 524,288. Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Full Road & Building Placement Guarantee:[/b] Solved engine-level ToolController collision bitmask limits (65,536 bits), allowing smooth placement of roads, bridges, tunnels, intersections, and buildings without tool lockups.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel) and Windows.
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments without frozen vehicles or phantom deadlocks.
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure custom traffic setups and extended networks reload perfectly.
[*] [b]Deep Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b] Seamless integration with Adaptive Roads, Network Skins, Node Controller Renewal, Move It, IMT, Network Multitool, Network Anarchy, Picker, Find It, etc.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins 2[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Picker[/b]
[*] [b]Find It 2[/b]
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Road Tools[/b]
[*] [b]Improved Public Transport 2 & 3[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Vehicle Options[/b]
[*] [b]More Vehicles Renew 2[/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote"		"v4.3.43 - TM:PE Crash Immunization, Full Feature Save/Load & 256-Frame NetAI Stepper: Fixed TM:PE IndexOutOfRangeException on loading segments >= 36864 by pre-expanding parkingAllowed and simulation arrays to 65024 via vanilla SerializableDataWrapper.LoadData (zero TM:PE hooks); preserved all TM:PE settings across savegames with binary Payload v2 (Timed Traffic Lights across all node ID combinations, Lane Connections, Speed Limits, Lane Arrows, Vehicle Restrictions, Junction Restrictions, Priority Signs, Parking Restrictions); fixed CustomSegmentLight reflection constructor; restored NetAI node and segment stepping to 256-frame cadence to eliminate vanilla traffic light gridlock and allow full traffic congestion color accumulation (bright red)."
